# SYNC(1M)

## NAME

sync - update the super block

## SYNOPSIS

```c
sync
```

## DESCRIPTION

*Sync* executes the *sync* system primitive. If the system is to be stopped, *sync* must be
called to insure file system integrity. See sync(2) for details.

## SEE ALSO

sync(2), update(8)
